ustom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T10:23:56-08:00","id":1433722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1421925-warding-stock-exchanges-prognostication-counter-strategies?p=1433715#post1433715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robin hood app is selling people's shares for them.<br /> <br /> So who's doing this. Syndicate IT division?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, Syndicate has an IT division: It's called Iteration X :P<br /> <br /> Or perhaps VA are doing this. Robin hood being a classic anty-system figure (rob the rich, give tot he poor), in spite of the fact he was actually the lord of the land, and was just stealing back what had been robbed to him in the first place<br /> <br /> Now, now. Robin Hood it's a polemical figure in the Syndicate. The actual robin existed in WoD, and was<i> a Craftmason</i>. Syndicate doesn't hate him, and sometimes use him as an example of someone who fougth for private property, but they also murdered his Convetion. They haven't any problem with the &quot;stealing to the rich&quot; because these rich were actual criminals, but they weren't exactly fans of the whole &quot;giving to the poor&quot; part either.<br /> <br /> [/tinfoil hat]&quot;GHASP&quot; Maybe the Craftmasons survived - their demise was overly exaggerated[/tinfoil hat] :P<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1433714-would-va-s-be-involved-with-the-gamestop-short-squeeze-in-the-wod?_=1611857861871\">There's a new thread about this, let's go talk this thing there.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-28-2021, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T17:09:35-08:00","id":1434060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1421925-warding-stock-exchanges-prognostication-counter-strategies?p=1433670#post1433670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such a ward would have to cover not just the stock market, but the whole world to some extent. Otherwise mages could scry the stock market *indirectly*. For instance, you could scry if a bussines it's going to be successful, instead of pointing towards the system itself. Not even the Technocracy can blind ALL the future, and because the &quot;free market&quot; covers a lot of activities in all kinds of places, I think this would be quite problematic.<br /> <br /> Also it's very important Syndicate magick *can* do the prognostications rigth because that's one of the things they want to sell to the people: That statistics, market research, etc - the tools inverstors use to predict the outcome - are better than praying a hail mary to win. But because these tools are given to sleepers, mages could incorporate them into their mojo to &quot;hack&quot; into this super big and costly ward.<br /> <br /> However, there could be cheaper countermeasures. A posibility - that would be very &quot;Syndicate&quot; - it's that they deliberately allow these kind of abuses to some extent, but have ways to scry them and control who get's to be megarich.<br /> <br /> Owning stock most likely counts as a sympathetic connection for the Syndicate uses of Data/Correspondence, so you're allready hooked in their net when you do that (and &quot;unhooking&quot; with magick would be pretty much screaming &quot;I'm a mage&quot; to anyone that searches, unless you're very, very, careful &amp; powerful). At the moment a wizard buys stock, they're already accepting to play the game of the Syndicate to a certain extent.<br /> <br /> After that point, it's a game of chiken. If you're a small player that just wants a little fun, they leave you be (they don't have the resources to catch every infraction). But if you try to win big, that will make ripples in the maket, and then the Syndicate will come to your door with one of those proposals you can't refuse. All mages know that, so they have to be very careful of not breaking the system</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. Stated another way:<br /> <br /> If the Syndicate warded the NASDAQ, someone could use Entropy or Time to predict the probabilities of Netflix doing well. If they warded Netflix, someone could use Entropy or Time to predict the probability of a pandemic then cross-reference that with the fact that Netflix does really well when people have to stay indoors. If they warded the probabilities of a pandemic, the Progenitors would probably get pissed at them for making everyone unable to notice that unsanitary conditions in Chinese wet markets combined with the fact that bats have incredible immune systems is a very bad thing.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, why would the Syndicate want to ward it when they could use it as a net to catch RDs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T17:33:38-08:00","id":1434062,"title":"","content":"Perhaps. On the other hand, the Syndicate is the least anti-RD of all of the Conventions, with the possible exception of the Void Engineers; they're more likely to try to co-opt RDs than to catch them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T04:39:55-08:00","id":1434105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1421925-warding-stock-exchanges-prognostication-counter-strategies?p=1434062#post1434062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps. On the other hand, the Syndicate is the least anti-RD of all of the Conventions, with the possible exception of the Void Engineers; they're more likely to try to co-opt RDs than to catch them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What can the Syndicate use to coopt RDs if RDs can so easily amass wealth?<br /> Syndicate &quot;Join us and we'll make you rich.&quot;<br /> RD &quot;Been there, done that. Nice system. Thanks.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T04:56:42-08:00","id":1434107,"title":"","content":"I was responding to the idea that the Syndicate <i>wouldn't</i> want to ward stock exchanges, in order to lure RDs in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T06:45:18-08:00","id":1434115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1421925-warding-stock-exchanges-prognostication-counter-strategies?p=1434062#post1434062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps. On the other hand, the Syndicate is the least anti-RD of all of the Conventions, with the possible exception of the Void Engineers; they're more likely to try to co-opt RDs than to catch them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you need to catch them in order to co-opt them.<br /> <br /> If you expect RDs are just going to walk into Syndicate offices with their CVs in hand, well...I don't think that's going to be very efficient. Among other things because the Technocracy it's a secret organization, and mages who know about it w/o being part of it probably are already in a hostile faction.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate needs to have ways to discover and target deviants. Isn't that what &quot;catch&quot; means in this context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-01-2021, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T13:46:57-08:00","id":1434178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1421925-warding-stock-exchanges-prognostication-counter-strategies?p=1434105#post1434105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can the Syndicate use to coopt RDs if RDs can so easily amass wealth?<br /> Syndicate &quot;Join us and we'll make you rich.&quot;<br /> RD &quot;Been there, done that. Nice system. Thanks.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while I don't think Syndicate should RDs allow to amass true fortunes before targeting them, your wording gave me a cruel idea.<br /> <br /> Been there, done that...migth be on point. Money can chage hands - it was made to do so.<br /> <br /> With Data, Entropy and PU even big fortunes can end bankrupt and liquidated. Let's remember that financial warfare it's the speciality of the Syndicate - a single rich RD most likely won't be able to oppose them. Infractors will see fortune eludes them. And most rich people can't stand being less rich, much less being actually poor. Money and privilege it's quite the drug, one day in a poor man's shoes and even magicians migth break.<br /> <br /> Now, this isn't the way the Syndicate likes to work. Forcing the enemy into submission it's more a NWO thing to do, and that's why room 101 it's so important.<br /> <br /> But it's still feasible, and I wouldn't put the Syndicate above such a tactic...after being *rejected*. Because we know what happens to the RDs that accept to work with the money club, but I don't think refusing it's <i>really</i> an option here. Especially not for a mage known to use prognostication to win at the &quot;casino&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-01-2021, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:05:10-07:00","id":1490167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1421925-warding-stock-exchanges-prognostication-counter-strategies?p=1432917#post1432917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ironically, the best way for the Traditions to fight state capitalism/Technocracy capitalism might be the free market... in the form of counter-economics, or more accurately, counter-Hypereconomics.<br /> <br /> Think about it: fiat currency was a hack on the gold standard. The Virtual Adepts are all about Reality Hacking. According to the Hypereconomics entry in M20, there are VA Hypereconomists. So, with those factors in mind, think about cryptocurrency, not just as a thing that exists, but also as a Virtual Adept project, an untraceable, untaxable, uncontrollable Reality Hack on Technocracy controlled fiat currencies. Given time (and some Adepts looking at Prime through a Syndicate lens), it could be used as a form of Primal Utility: the VA are all about the flow of information; cryptocurrencies are information flowing through the Internet, but they have the <i>potential</i> to be Quintessence moving through the Digital Web as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think that the modern Traditions would be down for playing the game that the Syndicate helped to invent. Remember - wealth is created by labor, and what backs the US dollar is not myth, but the actual labor and work of US workers. Statism and capitalism is the bedrock of Technocratic power, and I feel that various factions of the Traditions would work to uplift working people and endorse various kinds of anarchism and eco-socialism. Technocratic capitalism is literally killing the planet. Radical VAs and other Technomancers wouldnt be trying to become Technocrats themselves, but attacking the contradictions within capitalism. Also, I worked for 12 years in the financial sector, crypto is no different from foreign exchange. Crypto needs to be converted back and forth to fiat currency to have any value beyond the personal level and can't fund world wide capital finance, like international trade and credit, it's really a grift. The Syndicate likes Crypto because it lets them use the Consensus to bypass attacks on Primal Utility by the NWO. Of course the VA's will take advantage of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","user":"Robert Armsley","date":". 08-14-2022, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}